WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.102
JSON and YAML are ordinary formats, but they often sit directly on
security boundaries.

2
00:00:05.102 --> 00:00:15.789
Python applications use them for API requests, configuration files,
automation, CI/CD pipelines, cloud tooling, infrastructure definitions,
message queues, and data pipelines.

3
00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:24.891
When structured data changes program behavior, permissions, routing,
storage, or deployment settings, parsing becomes more than a convenience
feature.

4
00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:26.752
Structured data is still input.

5
00:00:26.752 --> 00:00:36.060
It may come from users, uploaded files, repositories, webhooks, third-
party systems, service responses, generated machine output, or internal
automation.

6
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:40.266
Some sources are more trusted than others, but trust should be explicit.

7
00:00:40.266 --> 00:00:47.230
A file being readable or a request being syntactically valid does not
prove that the content is safe for the application.

8
00:00:47.230 --> 00:00:55.090
Parsing, validation, deserialization, object mapping, configuration
loading, and business rule enforcement are different steps.

9
00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:57.710
Parsing turns bytes or text into a structure.

10
00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:01.640
Validation checks whether that structure matches expected rules.

11
00:01:01.640 --> 00:01:04.536
Object mapping places data into program objects.

12
00:01:04.536 --> 00:01:08.535
Business rules decide whether the result is meaningful and allowed.

13
00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:11.569
Skipping these distinctions creates fragile code.

14
00:01:11.569 --> 00:01:14.327
Valid JSON or valid YAML does not mean safe data.

15
00:01:14.327 --> 00:01:26.186
Risk themes include unsafe loaders, unexpected types, oversized input,
confusing numeric behavior, sensitive data exposure, mass assignment,
configuration mistakes, and parser resource pressure.

16
00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:37.080
Secure processing means treating structured data as untrusted until it has
been parsed safely, validated explicitly, bounded, mapped carefully, and
used only for its intended purpose.
